"Devices are `Arc`-wrapped for sharing across threads; streams are also `Arc`-"
"wrapped and can be passed to `.sync_on(&stream)` for explicit stream "
"scheduling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:232
msgid ""
"The default round-robin scheduling policy handles stream assignment "
"automatically for most workloads — these APIs are for when you need explicit "
"stream control (debugging, deterministic ordering, paired with "
"`AsyncKernelLaunch`, or overlapping compute with transfers on dedicated "
"streams)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:234
msgid ""
"The `borrow_raw` constructors do not take ownership of the underlying CUDA "
"handles and therefore do not destroy them on drop. They are `unsafe fn`s: "
"the caller guarantees the handles stay valid for as long as the borrow is "
"used. The `borrow_with_owner` variants keep an `Arc<dyn ForeignOwner>` alive "
"so the owning runtime's object cannot be dropped first. Use them when "
"integrating with another runtime that owns the context, stream, module, or "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:243
msgid "Kernel Launch Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:245
msgid "Several types configure how kernels compile and launch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:247
msgid ""
"**`CompileOptions`** — runtime overrides for entry-level "
"`optimization_hints`, typically used for autotuning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:249
msgid ""
"use cutile::tile_kernel::CompileOptions;\n"
"\n"
"let opts = CompileOptions::default()\n"
"    .occupancy(4)\n"
"    .num_cta_in_cga(2)\n"
"    .max_divisibility(16)\n"
"    .num_worker_warps_per_cta(4); // Bytecode 13.3+; use 4 or 8.\n"
"\n"
"let result = my_kernel(args).compile_options(opts).grid(grid).await?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:261
msgid ""
"Tile IR 13.4 restricts `num_worker_warps_per_cta` to 4 or 8. Tile IR 13.3 "
"accepts powers of two in `[1, 32]` (the assembler clamps to its supported "
"worker counts). The JIT checks the selected version's range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:265
msgid ""
"Different `CompileOptions` values trigger separate JIT compilations and are "
"part of the kernel cache key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/host-api.md:267
msgid ""
"Generated `#[cutile::entry]` launchers also expose launch-time configuration "
"methods:"
